{"slug": "kimchi-pancake", "nyt_id": 1014052, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014052-kimchi-pancake", "name": "Kimchi Pancake", "author": "Elaine Louie", "description": "Elaine Louie", "servings": {"text": "3 pancakes", "min": 3, "max": 3, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 tablespoon soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ teaspoon sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ teaspoon vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ teaspoon minced scallion", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "minced scallion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ teaspoon sesame seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sesame seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup flour", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup potato starch", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "potato starch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 egg", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "egg", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 scallions, cut into 1 ½-inch-long pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "cut into 1 ½-inch-long pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons garlic, sliced thinly", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "sliced thinly", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons Korean red pepper powder or ½ tablespoon cayenne", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "korean red pepper powder or ½ tablespoon cayenne", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 cup prepared cabbage kimchi, cut in 3-inch-long pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "prepared cabbage kimchi", "preparation": "cut in 3-inch-long pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 tablespoons kimchi juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "kimchi juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "6 tablespoons vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Make dipping sauce: In a small bowl, combine soy sauce, sesame oil, vinegar, scallion, sesame seeds and one-half tablespoon water. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, mix flour, potato starch and egg until smooth. Add scallions, garlic, red pepper powder, salt, kimchi and its juice. Mix well. Batter will be pale pink."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Place an 8- or 9-inch nonstick skillet over medium-high heat and add 1 tablespoon vegetable oil. When oil is hot, pour in one-third of the pancake batter. Fry until golden and crisp, about 3 to 4 minutes. Lift pancake with a spatula, add 1 tablespoon oil to pan and swirl it. Flip pancake and fry other side until golden, 2 to 3 minutes. Flip again, without adding oil, and fry for 1 minute. Flip one more time and fry 1 to 2 minutes. Pancake should be dark gold."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Repeat with remaining batter and oil, making 3 pancakes. Remove to a large round plate and cut each pancake into 6 wedges. Serve with dipping sauce."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 470.0, "protein_g": 6.4, "carbohydrates_g": 43.1, "fat_g": 30.8, "saturated_fat_g": 2.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.2, "cholesterol_mg": 53.3, "sodium_mg": 588.4, "fiber_g": 4.3, "sugar_g": 1.4, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["korean"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["all-purpose-flour", "kimchi", "potato-starch", "quick"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 87}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-01-13", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:07:56Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "kimchi-tuna-salad", "nyt_id": 1022166, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1022166-kimchi-tuna-salad", "name": "Kimchi Tuna Salad", "author": "Ali Slagle", "description": "Kimchi and canned tuna make a popular combination in Korean cooking. These two pantry staples are found together in a number of dishes like kimchi jjigae and kimbap, and here they are the basis of a lively, fortifying salad. Combine them with fresh ginger and celery for crunch (or an equal amount of other crunchy vegetables, like thinly sliced sugar snap or snow peas, radishes, carrot, cabbage or fennel). The dressing is made using the spicy liquid from the kimchi jar, rice wine vinegar and sesame oil, but because each jar of kimchi is different, you may want to tweak the seasonings to taste. Eat the salad on its own; with gim, or seaweed, as a hand roll; or with something starchy to balance the punch, like a burger bun, rice, boiled potatoes, soba or ramen noodles.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 10, "raw": {"total": "PT10M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 (16-ounce) jar cabbage kimchi, including juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "jar", "item": "cabbage kimchi", "preparation": "including juice", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons unseasoned rice wine vinegar, plus more to taste (or lemon or lime juice or 1 tablespoon fish sauce)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unseasoned rice wine vinegar", "preparation": "plus more to taste (or lemon or lime juice or 1 tablespoon fish sauce)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 teaspoons toasted sesame oil, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "toasted sesame oil", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "10 to 12 ounces canned tuna (preferably oil-packed), drained", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "canned tuna", "preparation": "drained", "optional": false, "quantity_max": 12.0}, {"position": 5, "raw": "6 celery stalks, thinly sliced crosswise (about 2 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "celery stalks", "preparation": "thinly sliced crosswise (about 2 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 (2-inch) piece fresh ginger, peeled and thinly sliced into less than ¼-inch-thick matchsticks", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "piece", "item": "fresh ginger", "preparation": "peeled and thinly sliced into less than ¼-inch-thick matchsticks", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Mayonnaise (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Red-pepper flakes, gochugaru or sambal oelek (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "red-pepper flakes", "preparation": "gochugaru or sambal oelek (optional)", "optional": true}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon toasted sesame seeds or furikake (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "toasted sesame seeds or furikake", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place a colander in a medium bowl and drain the kimchi. Coarsely chop the kimchi; you should have about 2 cups."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To the medium bowl with the kimchi juice, add the rice wine vinegar and sesame oil; stir to combine. Stir in the tuna and celery, breaking up the tuna into large chunks."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the chopped kimchi and ginger, and stir to combine. Because each batch of kimchi tastes different, it’s important to taste and adjust seasonings. If it needs more tang, add more rice wine vinegar. If it’s too intense, add more oil or even mayonnaise. If you want it spicier, add red-pepper flakes, gochugaru or sambal."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Serve with a sprinkle of sesame seeds, if desired. The salad keeps in the refrigerator for up to 3 days."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 124.0, "protein_g": 11.9, "carbohydrates_g": 6.6, "fat_g": 5.9, "saturated_fat_g": 0.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.8, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 19.8, "sodium_mg": 382.1, "fiber_g": 3.2, "sugar_g": 1.6, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-lunch-main-course-tuna-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["celery", "ginger", "kimchi", "quick", "tuna", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2021/05/03/dining/as-kimchi-tuna-salad/as-kimchi-tuna-salad-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "Ali Slagle’s kimchi tuna salad.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2021/05/03/dining/as-kimchi-tuna-salad/as-kimchi-tuna-salad-googleFourByThree-v2.jpg", "alt": "Ali Slagle’s kimchi tuna salad.", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2021/05/03/dining/as-kimchi-tuna-salad/as-kimchi-tuna-salad-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "Ali Slagle’s kimchi tuna salad.", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2021/05/03/dining/as-kimchi-tuna-salad/as-kimchi-tuna-salad-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Ali Slagle’s kimchi tuna salad.", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 1554}, "video_url": "https://vp.nyt.com/video/2024/07/09/120640_1_Kimchi-Tuna-Salad-Vertical-Video_wg_480p.mp4", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2021-05-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:40:54Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "kishke", "nyt_id": 1012814, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012814-kishke", "name": "Kishke", "author": "Joan Nathan", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "PT2H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "6 tablespoons chicken fat, suet or vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chicken fat", "preparation": "suet or vegetable oil", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 medium to large onion, cut in 1-inch pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium to large onion", "preparation": "cut in 1-inch pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 clove garlic, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 stalk celery, cut into chunks", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "stalk", "item": "celery", "preparation": "cut into chunks", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 large carrot, peeled and cut into chunks", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large carrot", "preparation": "peeled and cut into chunks", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup matzo meal", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "matzo meal", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon hot paprika", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "unit": "tsp", "item": "hot paprika", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat oven to 425 degrees. Line a baking sheet with a double layer of foil 12 inches long, topped with a sheet of parchment paper the same size."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a skillet over medium-low heat, heat 4 tablespoons fat or vegetable oil, and sauté onion and garlic until soft and golden. Cool slightly and pour everything, including fat, into a food processor equipped with a steel blade."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add remaining 2 tablespoons fat or oil, celery, carrot, matzo meal, salt, pepper and paprika to food processor. Pulse until vegetables and fat are incorporated into a paste. Transfer mixture to parchment paper, and shape into a knockwurst-like cylinder about 9 inches long and 1 ¾ inches in diameter. Enclose parchment and foil firmly around cylinder, folding ends under."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Bake for 30 minutes, then reduce heat to 350 degrees and cook until kishke is solid, 45 to 60 minutes more. Unroll kishke to expose surface; return to oven just until top is lightly browned and slightly crisped, 10 to 15 minutes. Cool slightly, and cut into rounds. If desired, serve as a side dish with pot roast or roast chicken."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 126.125, "protein_g": 1.0, "carbohydrates_g": 8.7, "fat_g": 9.7, "saturated_fat_g": 2.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.1, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 8.2, "sodium_mg": 115.5, "fiber_g": 0.9, "sugar_g": 1.3, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["eastern-european-jewish"], "diet": [], "course": ["side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["matzo-meal", "passover"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 70}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-10-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:34:12Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
